  "meta": {
    "title": "The Island With the Weirdest Border 🇸🇪🇫🇮🤯 Märket",
    "description": "Märket is a tiny rocky island in the Baltic Sea, split between Sweden 🇸🇪 and Finland (Åland) 🇫🇮 since 1809. In 1885 Finland built a lighthouse on it… on the Swedish side! 😅 In 1985 the two countries redrew the border into a strange zigzag, so the lighthouse ended up in Finland without either country losing any land 🤯 The border is marked by holes drilled in the rock, and it's checked every 25 years.",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "They moved a border instead of a lighthouse 🤯🇸🇪🇫🇮",
      "Would you visit Märket? 👇",
      "Which border should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
